namespace OpenTPW.UI.Original;

/// <summary>
/// Register of every UI value or rule that is not taken from original data or hard evidence
/// (docs/UI.md "Approximation register"). Each site carries a matching
/// <c>// [APPROX:UI-NNN]</c> comment; <see cref="LogOnce"/> reports them at startup.
/// </summary>
public static class UiApproximations
{
	public static readonly IReadOnlyList<(string Id, string Assumption, string EvidenceNeeded)> All = new[]
	{
		("UI-003", "button/arm state frames drawn at the root node pose; child translations ignored", "the PC UI mesh draw (the selected state mesh → local matrix → ancestor composition, not located in the PC round), or a capture of a button whose state child is offset"),
		("UI-004", "UI model triangles drawn back to front by Z, grouped per texture; the original's display object divides its depth buffer into a UI range in front of a linear and a log range (the dump 0x5833c0 prints [+0x48] begin, [+0x4c] ui end / linear begin, [+0x50] linear end / log begin, [+0x54] log end; the buffer itself is enabled or not, strings 0x768988 and 0x768958), which suggests depth-tested rather than sorted UI parts, not shown for the UI model draw", "the UI model draw call (which depth state and which order it submits) and whether the depth buffer is on for it"),
		("UI-006", "text colours: window titles and the lobby island name yellow, the object windows' labels and values white, the pause menu's lines cyan (white while focused), green values elsewhere, grey disabled, shadow and backdrop colours (the video's 720p chroma is good to about +-15 per channel); the original gives each text control an RGBA colour (0x65c5d5 → renderer +0x48, kept as ARGB at +0x78, 0x48fd07) and renders its glyphs white (0x48fa96) unless the control keeps the font's own colours (+0xdd); the values traced are the options labels' (0,0,0,255) (0x4a441e, UI-037), the buy list rows' (255,255,255,255) (0x4ad340), the pause menu lines' (0,175,190,255) (0x48b2b9) and the shared title colour (234,239,102,255) (0x492d20, fifteen window builders), with the lobby island name's second line (252,232,7,255) (0x4b8604) and a list row control that turns (140,0,60) on message 0x403 with a negative argument (0x4a0710); about a hundred more 0x65c5d5 calls (white, black, red (255,0,0) and (224,86,86) in the 0x4aa480 window) are not yet assigned to screens", "which screen each remaining 0x65c5d5 call colours (values, disabled states, costs) and the backdrop colours"),
		("UI-007", "one-pixel (×UI scale) drop shadow under UI text; the original's control text renderer (0x48f830) lays each string out and draws it once (one 0x6ae0f0 call into the control's bitmap), so its controls have no drop shadow; the whole glyph layout and draw library has one draw entry, 0x6ae0f0, whose only caller is the text box routine 0x492750 (three callers, each calling it once: the label and list text of 0x4a84c0 through 0x492c40, 0x480810 through 0x47fcd0 and 0x480460, 0x480570 through 0x47fe90; 0x6ae1c0 is the measure entry used by 0x4929f0), no offset or second pass exists there, and the BF4 glyphs carry only 0-15 coverage samples (docs/BF4-FONTS.md), so no shadow is baked into the font art; the capture's apparent shadow is not explained, and the vtable-reached control renderer 0x48f830 and the sprite blit of its bitmap (0x48f410) are not shown to add one", "the sprite draw of a text control's bitmap (0x48f410 → 0x588c20) and whether a capture's shadow is a render-state effect (UI-037)"),
		("UI-008", "text buttons on purple_button art: each half is one end cap, drawn with its mirror image; upper half normal, lower half focused/pressed", "capture of the original front-end buttons"),
		("UI-013", "the confirm dialog follows table 0x7583e8, the game-mode screen the name dialog 0x753f50 and the load screen the load dialog 0x7523f0, whose rows show the park's name and, right-aligned, the save file's local date and time as 0x49ec80 formats them (UITEXT 0x1c0 with day, month and year, then \" %02d:%02d\"; shipped parks and the sandbox have no file time and show none); the lobby's and the park's pause menus lay out their lines as 0x48c150 → 0x492f60 does (text width + 1 and height + 5 pixels on the canvas, centred, from top 10, 5 units apart), but the height follows OpenTPW's menu font tier ([EXT:ui-font-tier-by-scale]) with its text layout box standing in for the measure 0x4929f0, the online state's top of 0 (FUN_005b6450) is not followed and the focused line is plain white instead of the dark-grey-to-white ramp of 0x48b220", "the measure 0x4929f0 and the tick rate of the line message 0x1e"),
		("UI-018", "the lobby backdrop is painted flat with the cloud layer's eased colour (red toward the blue target) as a stand-in: the original clears to the fog colour 0x44DDFF and tints only its cloud layer (the engine sky's sky.tga, coloured from that grid), which is not drawn, nor is the scene's fog; two settings gate the eased colour and the flying-mesh count share, all in the .bss settings block 0x785840-0x785920 filled at runtime ([0x785888] > 1 and the options word 0x78d8d8 == 1 assumed to pass, as the capture's tinted clouds show; [0x7858dc] assumed 100 %, the video's flocks cannot be counted at 720p); an island without SKYCOLOUR gets black instead of the random target its constructor draws (0x5dfb4a-0x5dfb7b, three CRT rand() calls per island); the island clips are picked by a local stand-in for the C runtime's rand(); while the globe is up the lobby's flyers and island clips hold still (the original's behaviour there is not traced); the enter sequence is built (the camera turns to the island angle + π, the gate plays M1, the camera zooms under the black fade and the park starts below radius 8, 0x5e0490 states 1 and 2; an early leave's gate M2 close, 0x5e1350, is not reachable from the front end here); the key-unlock sequence is not traced; the lightning flash is not drawn (the capture shows none)", "the engine sky's draw (0x585ee0-0x586a00) and fog, the runtime contents of the settings block 0x785840-0x785920 and the options word 0x78d8d8, the lobby's subsystems while the globe is up, the key-award animation's code"),
		("UI-024", "the object windows (tables 0x755150, 0x755908, 0x755e80) draw their controls at the table rectangles, but b_move is not drawn (the move tool, mode 0x3b entered by 0x48cfa0, is not simulated) and the preview is OpenTPW's orthographic icon; the sideshow's winners gauge divides last month's winners by last month's customers where 0x4e1f20 sums the 30-entry daily histories at +0x1ac and +0x2bc, which OpenTPW does not keep; the shop and sideshow customer satisfaction gauges (0x4e1e30 over a 30-entry history at +0x3bc) are not simulated and draw empty, and the local happiness gauge counts the guests on park cells at the object's anchor cell where 0x4cd880 walks the thing lists of the cells around the thing's own cell; the build window lists a type with GoldenTicketCost above 0 that was not bought with tickets under its own name and its cash price where the original shows UITEXT 137 and the ticket cost negated (0x4ab034..0x4ab067), and fits the preview size to translated names and prices", "the move tool (mode 0x3b), the customer, winner and satisfaction histories and the buy list's ticket rows"),
		("UI-025", "the message tube holds up to five messages (not saved with the park) (the most the video shows) and drops the oldest on overflow; the panel's rectangles are table 0x7501a0; its action buttons take the mb_ model of their kind, but only the challenge offers carry actions (Accept and Decline) and which other original message uses which mb_ model is not traced; the strike messages (TAG_SYSTEM.str) and the challenge offers use the tube; its red body and white icons are OpenTPW's art ([EXT:message-tube-art]), an unanswered offer that was deleted is posted again ([EXT:challenge-offer-repost]) and OpenTPW's own feedback lines stay in a status line ([EXT:status-line])", "the original message queue (capacity, overflow, the events that post messages) and the mb_ model per message type"),
		("UI-026", "build icons: the preview model (P<name>.MD2, else the main model) is drawn by OpenTPW's CPU projection ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]); the buy window takes the original's 45° tilt (0x468e50), its turn of 0.0004 rad a millisecond that runs on across selections (0x46908a, 0x468e2f) and its fit (0x4689f0), but the original draws the preview through its 3D object pipeline (the ride object made by 0x463060 with a world matrix that 0x468e50 rebuilds each frame: the yaw and the ±π/4 tilt through the sine table, the matrix's x column scaled by 0.75 and its depth column by 0.1, then offsets) and starts the model's animation 5 (0x4732a0) and draws the footprint grid of the selected item (8×8 cells coloured by cell type) in control 0x1eb (0x4ab1b0), which OpenTPW does not; the object windows' previews keep a 30° tilt and 0.8 rad/s; sign faces use the object's rendered sign textures (ObjectSigns)", "the camera and projection the 3D pipeline draws the preview object with, the offset terms of 0x468e50 and the meaning of animation 5"),
		("UI-027", "a park click selects the original object occupying its grid cell; the original picks along the cursor ray: 0x45bf90 builds the ray from the mouse (0x790ac8/0x790acc), finds the terrain hit by the heightmap triangles, then marches the ray through the object cells (0x45cdc0: the cell's objects via 0x452ae0, a height-range test, then the model's triangles by 0x45d090), keeps the nearest hit of terrain and objects as the hovered object (0x469340, [0x7a1cd4]) and its hit point", "the ray-versus-model test 0x45d090 (which model and animation pose it uses) and the readers of the hovered object [0x7a1cd4] that make a left click select it; the selection then needs a ray pick against object geometry in OpenTPW (a build)"),
		("UI-031", "exactly Ctrl at the placing click keeps the build tool armed (0x5253b8) and at the last click of a ride's queue re-arms it, the tool's angle returns to 0 when it is left (0x52f3b6); the coaster and water-track tools, whose original sub-modes are not traced, end the build tool whatever the modifier, and the Ctrl tests at 0x5259e2/0x5259f4 are not mapped to an OpenTPW action; Level.PlaceObject owns purchase/guest linkage and its removal handler owns scrap credits", "what 0x52fab0 tests (an entrance or queue, medium confidence) and the coaster and track sub-modes' continuation"),
		("UI-032", "catalogue names greedily wrap in their slots; the original's formatter (0x6aec80) wraps greedily: a line ends at the last break opportunity (glyph flag 0x10) before the glyph that overflows the width, dropping trailing spaces (flag 2), or before that glyph when the line has none; longer single-line labels fall back to the small font ([EXT:fit-button-text])", "which characters the formatter flags as break opportunities and spaces, and whether the catalogue slots are multi-line text controls"),
		("UI-034", "a fully opaque texture on a transparent (flag 0x2) model slot keys out black with a soft edge: transparent up to channel 6, opaque from 48, alpha ramped and colour un-premultiplied between (only ipan in the lobby f_lobbutbg panel)", "the original's render state for flagged texture slots"),
		("UI-036", "options slider: ball centre moves linearly over the track for value index 0..steps-1; click/drag sets the nearest step (OpenTPW's own steps, [EXT:options-slider-steps]); the original's slider class (vtable 0x705b20) places the thumb at track left + (value - min) × (track width - thumb width) / (max - min) in integer units (0x66b088), sets the value from a drag as min + the truncated (thumb left - track left) × (max - min) / (track width - thumb width) (0x66af19), moves one page (+0x148, default 1 from 0x66adc9) toward a click on the track (0x66b8aa) and one step on its arrows (message 0x100) or by the wheel delta (0x1000d); the options page gives its sliders the range 0..100 (0x4a455a) and sets the resolution and quality sliders to index × 50 (0x4a3d02, 0x4a3d23); the options page's change handler (0x4a2e90) turns the slider value v into the resolution index (v × 2) / 100 (0x423b60) and the quality index (k × v) / 100 with k 2, or 1 while the options word 0x78d8d8 is 0 (0x423ba0), and passes the music, effects and speech sliders on as the raw 0..100 volume (0x51bba0, 0x51bb80, 0x51bbc0, 0x423b40) without snapping the knob", "the knob's position after a drag for the 0..100 volume sliders and what a track click does there"),
		("UI-037", "option bar label colour (16,16,48), no drop shadow; the original's options labels (0x4a43b0) and slider labels (0x4a4490) are text controls given the colour (0,0,0,255) (0x4a441e, 0x4a44fe) and font slot 6 ([0x7537b4]) and drawn once without a shadow (0x48f830); how the control's colour reaches the white glyph bitmap (0x48fa96) when it is drawn is not traced, so the capture's near-black is kept", "the sprite draw of the control's text bitmap (0x48f410 → 0x588c20) and whether it tints with the colour at +0x78"),
		("UI-039", "option label size follows OpenTPW's fit rule ([EXT:option-label-fit]: letter box about 58 % of the label rectangle height, shared per page, a label whose widest value does not fit drops alone to the largest size that does); the original's options labels take font slot 6 of the bank ([0x7537b4], 0x4a443c: GAME5AA/GAME7/GAME8/GAME9 for banks 0-3) and their setup (0x4a43b0) does no fitting", "what the original does with a label that overflows (UI-032)"),
		("UI-041", "Load Park takes no game type from the loaded park: the original derives GameType from flag bits 0x2000000/0x1000000 of 0x7a1a8c (0x550ca0), set by a front-end toggle (0x4bbf63), and the Mac saves none with a park", "whether a park file of the PC build can carry the game type (not traced)"),
		("UI-042", "the camera button's slide-out panel (table 0x751720) slides in and out as the arm drawer 0x4a14f0 does (ten 20 ms steps, cat_ui 0x1C and 0xC2, help 0x131), but its slide ends at the table rectangle where the original ends at the HUD window's right + 50 with the panel centred on the arm (0x4a15d2-0x4a1650); the camcorder button arms the C-key walk ([EXT:camcorder-first-person]) where the original's button 99 enters the camcorder at once (0x498ad0 → 0x481a10), and the walk's movement and look controls are not traced (the original's eye is terrain + 5 units, 0x42b1c0); the postcard window (table 0x7540d8) keeps its photo frame empty and its preview and address book buttons disabled (the 640×240 camcorder photo 0x4a9280, the preview redraw 0x4a84c0 and the address book 0x4a8140 are not ported); the view cycle is a third button ([EXT:camera-view-cycle])", "the HUD window's rectangle; the walk's key bindings (action table 0x787c14) and the time unit of its turn step; the photo, its preview and the address book"),
		("UI-044", "buy window list rows are 41.4 units high (measured at 720p, +-1 unit), ten rows show and the wheel scrolls one row; the original's pitch is the height of the list's first row control (0x663718 via 0x65d865, frame insets removed), which the row factory 0x4ad240 makes once from font slot 7's line height (BF4 header byte 5, 0x6b05e0) × 1536 / screen height + 6 (cached at 0x7cc200): 42 at 512×384 (GAME6AA, 9), 41 at 640×480 (GAME8, 11), 39 at 800×600 (GAME9, 13) and 34 at 1024×768 (GAME10, 14); the loans list's row factory 0x4a02b0 uses the same rule, so its rows take the same pitch; OpenTPW keeps the measured pitch because its output sizes have no original font bank", "a bank rule for OpenTPW's output sizes (UI-002)"),
		("UI-046", "the gauge bars (buy, ride, shop and sideshow windows) take the original's values and shape: the integer (value << 10) / 100 of a 0..1024 range (0x4abb00, 0x4ade40), a bar of the control's cell less 10 units top and bottom (0x485e30) that shows the art cut off at the value with the rest of the cell the track (0x478400: ridestatbar.wct's top 16 texel rows the bar, its bottom 16 the track); the colours of the bar and the track are read off the 720p video (a 70 % bar runs red, orange, yellow to lime green), because the art ridestatbar.wct (32 x 32 after OpenTPW's wavelet decode: rows 0-15 a gradient from dark olive through yellow (225,255,0) to green (119,255,0), rows 16-31 a grey track) has no red end (its happygrad.wct has blue texels at the left), so the video's red-to-orange start comes from a decode difference, a tint or vertex colours that are not read", "why the decoded ridestatbar.wct differs from the rendered bar: the wavelet decoder (TextureFile) or the tint or vertex colours of the gauge sprite (0x477ff0)"),
		("UI-047", "which OpenTPW tool state corresponds to the mode-object types that show control 48: type 3 (the tool-mode object, vtable 0x6fe9e0) wraps every build tool, so the held blueprint's price, the path or queue line's cost so far and the coaster track segment under the cursor show it; type 8 is the coaster panel's mode object (vtable 0x6feaa0, built by 0x46cfc0 when a panel button is pressed, 0x497bc0), which shows it only while bit 0 of 0x79c658 is set (0x447990; set at 0x441a5d), a coaster sub-state OpenTPW does not track, so OpenTPW shows the coaster cost in every sub-mode; no mode-object class returns type 4 (the classes 0x6fe980-0x6fead0 return 7, 3, 1, 5, 6, 8 and 9; 5 and 6 are the staff place and carry tools), and the staff and patrol tools show nothing", "what bit 0 of 0x79c658 stands for in the coaster tool"),
		("UI-050", "the buy list's third column draws a tick box per row, ticked when the park owns at least one of the item; the box and the tick are drawn with rectangles and strokes in the video's colours, not the original's art (i_boxtick.MD2 holds only the empty box)", "the original tick art and the unnamed control 491"),
		("UI-051", "the ticket counter is the park's available tickets, where the original shows the player's earned tickets less the spent count (0x5af5d0), because an in-park ticket purchase does not reach the player ledger", "an in-park ticket purchase recorded in the player ledger"),
		("UI-060", "finance graph line colours, scaling and default selected series use the tracked monthly ledger values", "original financial graph capture and its sample/render handler"),
		("UI-064", "the research workload knob is the original's slider: values 1023 (top) to 0 (bottom), a limit of ((100 - c) / 3 + c) x 1024 / (MaxResearchersInPark x the grade-4 ResearchAbility) from the researchers' summed ability c, a workload of 70 + 30 x value / limit and the ball's travel (0x4a96b0, 0x4aac80, 0x66b088); the pointer sets the value whose ball centre lies under it, which stands in for the slider class's own pointer handling; the knob's child 0xd2d12 (set to the limit) and 0xd2d11 (state (2 x step) / 7) are not drawn; the slider's ball proc 0x66bb9b moves the ball by the pointer's offset from the press point (stored per button at 0x10005 in 0xfaa59a/0xfaa59c) from the rectangle saved at the press or release (0x65cf3d), clamped to the track by 0x66b771, then reads the value back with 0x66af19, where OpenTPW centres the ball under the pointer", "what 0xd2d12 and 0xd2d11 draw, and whether the saved rectangle is the press-time ball"),
		("UI-066", "the research fluids step at a fixed 30 ticks a second; the original advances each panel's fluid (0x4a9fc0) on every message 0x1e, which the UI sends once per rendered frame (0x48a580 → 0x658f6c)", "the original's frame rate"),
		("UI-080", "staff list has ten equal rows in the table content area, where the video's hire list (12:00) has a pitch of about 19 px at 720p (about 40 units, not 47) and so shows about twelve rows: the original list class takes its row pitch from its font's text height (0x663718: 0x65d865 into +0x170) and shows (bottom - top) / pitch rows (0x663786); the wheel's one row per notch is the original's (0x665c35, 0x46b600)", "the staff list font's text height"),
		("UI-081", "applicant details: the skill gauge is a type-9 gauge set to the candidate's grade byte (+8, written by 0x507600 as AvgGradeOf* + R % 3 - 1 stored as 4 when above 4, OpenTPW's Grade) x 1024 / 5 (0x49b8e2) of its 0..1024 range (0x66d885 clamps), so a grade-0 candidate's value is 0; OpenTPW fills (Grade + 1) / 5 because the video's cheapest ($60) candidate shows about a fifth (12:00); the gauge models crop their art to value × 100 / 1024 per cent (UI-046), so a byte of 0 draws an empty bar and the fifth is not explained by the drawing", "which byte the video's cheapest candidate holds (the writer 0x507600 stores AvgGradeOf* + R % 3 - 1 as a byte, a wrapped 0xff becoming 4)"),
		("UI-082", "the hire window's figure is drawn one sprite pixel to 3.2 canvas units (640 pixels across the 2048-unit canvas), where the original sets its register 8 to 8.0 (0x004755D0, the scale 0x00542010 copies to the draw record +0x2C, default 1.0); how the screen-sprite path (flag 0x40000, list 0x0087692C) turns that scale into pixels is not traced; the figure also shows for an employee selected in the employed view, where 0x49BA00 reads only the applicant pool (0x507BD0, 32 entries of 0x14 bytes)", "the engine's screen-sprite quad size, or a capture of the hire window and of the employed view"),
		("UI-086", "paths, queues and placed objects use plain coloured cells over the shipped theme map image; the original colours each cell from tables at 0xf86a28-0xf86c20 that are filled at run time (the per-object colours through 0x5f09a0 from a value) and outlines a cell where its neighbour differs (0x5f2380); the base colours are immediates written by 0x5f0700 (black, white, green, yellow, blue (0,78,254), cyan, dark blue (11,66,110) and gradient triples built by 0x5f0970), and the draw 0x5f2380 switches on the cell kind (1 path, 2 queue, 3 object, 8 ...) with the layer mask at +0x18, taking an object cell's colour from 0x5f09a0 over the gradient of the value read from the thing (0x4e0860, 0x4e1e30 by layer mode 2 or 3)", "which table entry and gradient value each cell kind and layer mode of 0x5f2380 uses, and the outline rule"),
		("UI-091", "the locator panels take staff newest first (by id, descending) and visitors by id, where the original walks the role's thing list (+0x210) and the thing list (0x4824d0); the camera snaps to the followed actor every frame where the original eases it (0x486860); a staff member's patrol rectangle is not marked (0x536100 in 0x4b3640); the panels appear without sliding and without the sounds 0xc6 / 0x11f; a picked-up member's state frame 9 (0x485ec0) draws the first frame; the staff window's own locate buttons focus actual actor positions, the list rows' 0x402 path (0x4867b0) is the original's; the visitor info window that Ctrl+V tests ([0x7cc418], window object 0x7cc408) is not ported: a left click on an All Visitors row or a visitor picked in the park stands in for opening it and it closes with the All Visitors window, where the original's stays open on its own", "the order of the role lists, the easing of 0x486860 and the patrol markers"),
		("UI-092", "the per-employee window (table 0x756f48, 0x4b6080) shows the role's name in its portrait frame where the original plays a live figure of the employee (0x4b5330 → 0x486530); a click on the title does not rename (0x48d2e0, help 85); the help 0xd4 the window posts while the employee has a patrol area (0x4b5ab0) is not posted; the arrows cycle the economy's member list in hire order for the thing list (0x7cf56c, newest first); the locate button is disabled while the employee has no world position (held in the hand), where 0x4b5f07 always opens the locator panel", "drawing the figure, porting the rename dialog, and the thing-list order of staff loaded from a save"),
		("UI-094", "the ride view is a first-person eye on the camera car of the coaster train with the smallest position (the car 0x436880 selects) or the carriage's height (prototype), looking along the track or the entry heading; the field of view is 55 where the original's projection (0x578be0) is built with the argument 90 at its two initialisation sites (0x42a990, 0x54e860) and never changed by the ride camera, but how its scales and the viewport (0x5781d0) turn that into an angle for OpenTPW's camera is not traced; the signs of the free-look rotations come from the video; the static lasts 0.33 s (video 0.30-0.35 s)", "the static's timer and the projection's x and y scales against the viewport (0x578be0, 0x5781d0, 0x46f6f0's rotation signs)"),
		("UI-095", "leaving the ride view restores its prior camera instance, including the host terrain walk, and re-centres the host park camera on the object under its target with the original's test (0x42a340: a placed object whose type has CannotRide 0) and look direction (0x42a1d0: the link byte of the object's cell masked with 0x55); the original's park camera is its own pose (yaw, height and smoothing in 0x42b1c0) that OpenTPW's host camera does not reproduce, and whether the original's object cells carry a link byte at all is not traced (OpenTPW's cell map keeps link bytes for path, queue and track cells only, so the yaw rule fires for none of the placed objects)", "the link byte of an object's map cell (the writers of +0xd outside paths, queues and tracks) and the park camera's own pose"),
		("UI-096", "the pause menu (with the screens opened from it) and the map window stop the park simulation; the pause menu's cases 1 and 22 open 0x49efb0 and case 2 0x49f280 and case 5 0x4a3a30 (jump table 0x48bbc8 of 0x48b6a0), which keep the pause (0x49efba, 0x49f29f, 0x4a3a6c), so those callers are covered; the postcard (0x4a93d7, Ctrl+P) and the delete confirmations (the message box 0x47f020 of 0x48cd10) pause too, but the other generic message boxes (table 0x74f920, up to three b_okay/b_exit buttons, 27 call sites in 7 functions: the alert queue 0x47f620 fed through 0x47f410, the file errors of 0x4237f0, 0x4a77f0, the online notices 0x4bc500 and 0x4ec030; each pauses at 0x47f26c while the gate 0x786ba4 is 1 and 0xf82884 is 0) and the application's deactivation (WM_ACTIVATEAPP in the main window procedure 0x46b600, 0x46b74c, while 0xf82884 is 0) do not", "which of OpenTPW's other dialogs (the dismissal box, whose original 0x4b5e5d is no 0x47f020 caller, the loan boxes, the restart and quit boxes) correspond to the remaining 0x47f020 call sites, and pausing for focus loss"),
		("UI-100", "the link and end pointers are never chosen and the cash pointer is not chosen at 0x539fb6: end (0x816d4c) is set when the path validator 0x535670 returns code 0xb (0x535ae5, 0x535b3d) and at 0x53a1c6, link (0x816d60) by 0x535670 at 0x535c72 and for code 8, a queue end whose neighbour is of kind 3 (0x535d00), and cash (0x816d5c) also at 0x539fb6; the crosshair's art (CCro.tga) is not in the game data", "the path and queue states behind the validator codes 8 and 0xb, the cash pointer of the tool at 0x539fb6 and the crosshair art"),
